<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28969" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mē^trĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετρικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to
			measuring</i> or <i>measure</i> (postAug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leges metricae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 88, § 219</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>of</i> or <i>relating to
				metre, metrical</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metrici pedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 52</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">48</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mē^trĭcus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a prosodian</i>
			(post-class.), <i><span class="en">Gell. 18, 15, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
